> 
> If "lo birje" is "a beer", then we need a way to say plain "beer".
> Massifiers erase individuating boundaries, and that's what we need
> here.

"loi birje" does that. "lo birje" == a (quantity of) beer. "loi
birje" == beer.

Also, "lei birje" isn't neccesarily always wrong, as xod was saying,
either. If you have 3 bottles of beer, and are calling each "le
birje", you can massify them normally as "lei birje". (actually
he was talking about djacu. But djacu, birje, what's the difference)

